## 2. Educational content

Educational content includes, without limitation:

- Markdown lessons under `src/content/lessons/markdown/`
- Diagrams under `src/content/lessons/diagrams/`
- Curriculum, glossary, and resource metadata under `src/content/`
- Related educational copy on public pages (About, Home, etc.)

### Grant

Unless otherwise noted in a specific file, educational content is provided
**free of charge for personal learning and non-commercial educational use**.

You may:

- Read, share links to, and study the materials
- Quote short excerpts with attribution and a link back to this project
- Use the materials in free classroom or community study sessions with attribution

You may **not**, without prior written permission:

- Sell the content as a paid product or paid course pack
- Remove attribution or present the content as solely your original work
- Republish the full lesson corpus (or a substantial portion) as a competing
  commercial dataset or mirror

### Attribution

When you share or adapt short excerpts, please credit:

**AI Vibe Coding Master** — free educational project

and link to the project site when practical.

### Third-party material

Quotations, trademarks, and document titles from third parties (for example
MDN, Git, Next.js, MCP, OpenAI, and other vendors) remain the property of their
respective owners. Short quotations are used for education with links to the
original sources. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` and the in-lesson source links.

### AI assistance

Some materials were organized with assistance from AI tools. Human review is
used to improve accuracy, but content may still contain errors. See the site
Terms and About pages.

### No warranty

All content is provided “AS IS” without warranty of any kind. It is not legal,
security, or professional advice. Always verify against official documentation
and your own tests before production use.

